#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:14 941a4fd03c294960a9d3bd16a50a7c02
msgid "Qubes Desktop showing windows from different qubes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:19 8ad57c08e88d40e8829c310b25ef95c8
msgid ""
"In this example, the word processor runs in the “work” :term:`qube`, which "
"has been assigned the “blue” label. It is fully isolated from other qubes, "
"such as the “untrusted” qube (assigned the “red” label – “Watch out!”, "
"“Danger!”) used for random Web browsing, news reading, as well as from the "
"“work-web” qube (assigned the “yellow” label), which is used for work-"
"related Web browsing that is not security critical. These applications run "
"in different qubes each of which has its own X server, filesystems, etc. "
"Notice the different color frames (labels) and qube names in the titlebars. "
"These are drawn by the trusted Window Manager running in Dom0, and apps "
"running in qubes cannot fake them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:25 ec804c55d44144fa89ac417d67f94a7d
msgid "Qubes Desktop showing use of qubes running Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:30 64719649eb2a40d6b00c5c6f81a8fa41
msgid ""
"Qubes can also run Windows qubes in seamless mode, integrated into the "
"common Qubes trusted desktop, just like Linux qubes! (Seamless GUI "
"integration was introduced in Qubes R2 Beta 3.) This requires :doc:`Qubes "
"Windows Tools </user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools>` to be installed "
"in the Windows qube first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:36 0bc70c63332845cb85958322fb9ead28
msgid "Qubes Desktop showing inter qube file copy in Windows qubes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:41 d4efce2c1d374a1a9824f23cf856cc1f
msgid ""
"Windows qubes are fully integrated with the rest of the Qubes OS system: "
"this includes things such as secure, policy governed, inter-qube file copy, "
"clipboard, and generally our whole elastic qrexec infrastructure for secure "
"inter-qube RPC! Starting with Qubes R2 Beta 3 Qubes also supports HVM-based "
"templates, allowing you to instantly create many Windows qubes with a shared "
"“root filesystem” from the Template (you should ensure your license allows "
"for such instantiation of the OS in the template). Just like with Linux "
"qubes!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:46 04e86e2fcd79445dbfb17dad1140d088
msgid "Each window shows the name and color of the qube."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:51 e543af20887e457ba2f874b049183c74
msgid ""
"You can always see clearly to which qube a given window belongs. Here it’s "
"immediately clear that the passphrase-prompting window belongs to some qube "
"with the “blue” label. When we look at the titlebar, we see “[qubes]”, which "
"is the name of the actual qube. Theoretically, the untrusted application "
"(here, the red Tor Browser running in a :term:`disposable`) beneath the "
"prompt window could draw a similar looking window within its contents. In "
"practice, this would be very hard, because it doesn’t know, e.g., the exact "
"decoration style that is in use. However, if this is a concern, the user can "
"simply try to move the more trusted window onto some empty space on the "
"desktop such that no other window is present beneath it. Or, better yet, use "
"the Expose-like effect (available via a hot-key). A malicious application "
"from an untrusted qube cannot spoof the whole desktop because the trusted "
"Window Manager will never let any qube “own” the whole screen. Its titlebar "
"will always be visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:57 e4fd541208664a0f9f635fb455256dcb
msgid "Tray icons include icons from qubes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:62 2aed4c67702b4f0f85503993a79e1c25
msgid ""
"Qubes is all about seamless integration from the user’s point of view. Here "
"you can see how it virtualizes tray icons from other qubes. Notice the "
"network icon is in red. This icon is in fact managed by the Network Manager "
"running in a separate :term:`net qube`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:69 e6a8b182b6cb4ee3bfbb148c8b1e287c
msgid ""
"Qubes desktop showing networking prompt from the net qube, identifiable by "
"color and name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:74 deb930cdadbc4ff0a1bdb938d8e087e2
msgid ""
"All the networking runs in a special, unprivileged net qube. (Notice the red "
"frame around the Network Manager dialog box on the screen above, which "
"reflects the color assigned to the net qube.) This means that in the event "
"that your network card driver, Wi-Fi stack, or DHCP client is compromised, "
"the integrity of the rest of the system will not be affected! This feature "
"requires Intel VT-d or AMD IOMMU hardware (e.g., Core i5/i7 systems)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:80 86fa0d2f6caa4bdab4500fa0281acab2
msgid ""
"Qubes Update Tool shows templates that may need updating, and allows you to "
"select which will be updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:84 d2d8b60f79c64c47b6df4cbd85b473e1
msgid ""
"Qubes lets you update all the software in all the qubes all at once, in a "
"centralized way. This is possible thanks to Qubes’ unique template "
"technology. Note that the user is not required to shut down any AppVMs "
"(qubes) for the update process to run. This can be done later, at a "
"convenient moment, and separately for each qube."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:90 0a13ea0df5a64b11877f2aa892859508
msgid ""
"Qubes desktop showing information window about data securely copied to the "
"global clipboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:95 604f9baed5634b7fb084e1c9d444609d
msgid ""
"Qubes supports secure text copy-and-paste operations between qubes. Only the "
"user can initiate a copy or paste operation using a special key combination "
"(Ctrl-Shift-C/V). Other qubes have no access to the clipboard buffer, so "
"they cannot steal data from the clipboard. Only the user decides which qubes "
"should be given access to the clipboard. (This is done by selecting the "
"destination qubes’ window and pressing the Ctrl-Shift-V combination.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:101 da894eefa126423896f57407a8dd29a2
msgid "Qubes desktop showing use of menu to copy file to global clipboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:106 ddbb3fd730104fafafa894c061075142
msgid ""
"Qubes desktop showing security prompt when pasting file from global clipboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:110 220f2d3df762419d928aa2d49df7dcfb
msgid "Qubes also supports secure file copying between qubes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:116 63cdef5a154647469f44282aec67603a
msgid "Menu showing option to edit file in disposable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:121 369ec2f99dfe46848697b89fe9db1c7f
msgid ""
"Qubes desktop showing source qube and disposable with file open for editing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:126 0db216bcdda747138c635b668b15f4ee
msgid ""
"Qubes' unique :term:`disposable` qubes allow the user to open any file in a "
"disposable in a matter of seconds! A file can be edited in a disposable, and "
"any changes are sent back to the original file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:131 c9aea585844c47ccab9b24ce4750d6ee
msgid "File manager menu with option to convert a file to a trusted PDF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:136 804bce8f677b41a08a4ace0dd090d76e
msgid "Qubes desktop showing progress bar for PDF conversion process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:140 498f48590bea47baa1d0ef62e94def31
msgid ""
"Qubes provides an advanced infrastructure for programming inter-qube "
"services, such as a PDF converter for untrusted files (which is described in "
"`this article <https://blog.invisiblethings.org/2013/02/21/converting-"
"untrusted-pdfs-into-trusted.html>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:146 afd09760abec4f629945eed72e60d528
msgid "GUI showing how firewall rules can be edited for a qube"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/screenshots.rst:150 6beff7de5a5945d29dbbeef4593ef3de
msgid ""
"Qubes provides a dedicated firewall that itself runs in an isolated "
"FirewallVM."
msgstr ""

